---
/**
 * TEMPLATE for a custom-designed field note. Copy, rename, edit.
 *
 * Use this only when a note needs its own look. Notes that read fine in the
 * site's standard card layout stay as plain `.md` in `src/content/cards/` —
 * this path costs more to maintain, so it should earn it.
 *
 * Wiring (see website/README.md → "Custom-designed field notes"):
 *   1. Copy this file to `<PascalCaseName>.astro` in this folder.
 *   2. Create `src/content/cards/<slug>.mdx` with `display: bare` in the
 *      frontmatter, then import and render this component from its body.
 *   3. Pick a unique root class (`.note` below → e.g. `.vanity`) and prefix
 *      every class in the file with it. Scoping protects you from other
 *      notes, but a unique prefix keeps the file readable.
 *
 * Rules that are not obvious, all of which have already broken a build here:
 *
 *   - Frontmatter key is `display`, NOT `layout`. MDX reserves `layout` and
 *     resolves it as a component import; using it fails the build with
 *     `Rollup failed to resolve import "bare"`.
 *   - Keep `<style>` scoped. Do NOT add `is:global`. Global rules from one
 *     note leak into every other bare note and into present mode.
 *   - `.note` is full-bleed and paints the page background; `.note-inner` is
 *     the reading column. Setting a background on `body` requires a global
 *     rule, so don't — paint it here instead.
 *   - In SVG, a CSS rule beats a presentation attribute. If you write
 *     `<text text-anchor="start">` and any CSS sets `text-anchor`, the CSS
 *     wins and your labels silently shift and clip. Set SVG paint and
 *     geometry-adjacent properties (`text-anchor`, `stroke-width`, `fill`)
 *     from classes, not attributes, or mirror the attribute in CSS.
 *   - Give every `<svg>` a `role="img"` and an `aria-labelledby` `<title>`
 *     describing what the diagram shows, not what it looks like.
 *   - Long labels inside an SVG cannot wrap and will clip on a narrow screen.
 *     Put prose in HTML (`<figcaption>`) and keep SVG text to a few words.
 *   - Check the page at 390px wide before opening a PR. Field notes get
 *     opened on phones and projected in rooms, rarely read at desk width.
 */
---

<div class="note">
  <div class="note-inner">
    <section class="note-hero">
      <p class="note-kicker">Field note · topic</p>
      <h1>The claim, stated short</h1>
      <p class="note-dek">One sentence that gives away the conclusion.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="note-card">
      <p class="note-num">01</p>
      <h2>One idea per section</h2>
      <p>
        Two or three sentences. If a section needs more, it is two sections.
      </p>

      <figure class="note-fig">
        <!-- Diagram here. Prose belongs in the figcaption, not the SVG. -->
        <figcaption>What the reader should take from the picture.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="note-close">
      <p class="note-num">The job</p>
      <p class="note-shout">The line you want them to remember.</p>
    </section>

    <footer class="note-foot">
      <p class="note-back">
        <a href="/field-notes/">← All field notes</a>
        <a href="/">aleberriz.com</a>
      </p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .note {
    --accent: #4cc9f0;
    --dim: #6b7688;
    --rule: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.09);

    min-height: 100vh;
    color: #ccd5e0;
    background: #06080c;
    font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .note-inner {
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.25rem 4rem;
  }

  .note p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .note a { color: var(--accent); }

  .note-kicker,
  .note-num,
  .note-back {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--dim);
  }

  .note-hero { padding: 4.5rem 0 3.5rem; }
  .note-hero h1 {
    margin: 1.25rem 0 1.5rem;
    font-family: Fraunces, Georgia, serif;
    /* clamp() keeps the headline readable at 390px without a media query */
    font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 11vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #fff;
  }
  .note-dek { font-size: 1.2rem; color: #aebacb; max-width: 34ch; }

  .note-card,
  .note-close {
    padding: 3rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .note-card h2 {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1.25rem;
    font-family: Fraunces, Georgia, serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 7.5vw, 2.3rem);
    line-height: 1.12;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .note-fig { margin: 1.75rem 0; }
  .note-fig svg { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
  .note-fig figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--dim);
  }

  .note-shout {
    font-family: Fraunces, Georgia, serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 8.5vw, 2.7rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .note-foot {
    padding: 2.5rem 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .note-back { display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; }
</style>
